Adeline Kerner and Elise Saliba.

897
01:42:05,018 --> 01:42:08,458
So what is the topic of this talk? We are

898
01:42:08,518 --> 01:42:12,458
particularly interested in the data generated during the use

899
01:42:12,518 --> 01:42:13,998
of identification tools.

900
01:42:14,918 --> 01:42:18,478
Our main questions is quite simple: Can we

901
01:42:18,638 --> 01:42:22,358
use an exchange standard such as SDD, not

902
01:42:22,398 --> 01:42:26,238
only to share identification keys, but also to record and

903
01:42:26,318 --> 01:42:29,498
share the way these keys are used?

904
01:42:37,278 --> 01:42:40,478
Identification tool based on morphological data

905
01:42:41,238 --> 01:42:43,318
have changed considerably over time,

906
01:42:44,278 --> 01:42:47,458
from

907
01:42:47,658 --> 01:42:50,358
identification of specimen with single access key,

908
01:42:51,258 --> 01:42:51,678
where

909
01:42:52,558 --> 01:42:55,478
the user follow a predefined sequence of questions,

910
01:42:56,438 --> 01:42:58,918
then interactive free access key,

911
01:42:59,998 --> 01:43:03,898
which provide more flexibility. The user can choose which character

912
01:43:03,938 --> 01:43:07,258
to examine next, depending on what can be observed on the

913
01:43:07,338 --> 01:43:07,978
specimen.

914
01:43:08,918 --> 01:43:10,678
More recently, automatic

915
01:43:11,898 --> 01:43:15,718
AI identification tools based on images or sounds.

916
01:43:16,578 --> 01:43:19,498
And now, I read identifications,

917
01:43:20,738 --> 01:43:24,118
as explained just before by Agathe Puissant.

918
01:43:25,542 --> 01:43:29,022
So today, there are several ways of

919
01:43:29,082 --> 01:43:32,862
identifying an organism, and consequently several

920
01:43:33,222 --> 01:43:36,742
types of information that can be generated during the

921
01:43:36,822 --> 01:43:38,482
identification process.

922
01:43:41,262 --> 01:43:45,062
And identification tools are also used in many different

923
01:43:45,122 --> 01:43:48,782
contexts: research, education and training,

924
01:43:49,022 --> 01:43:52,842
citizen science program, activities with general public,

925
01:43:53,342 --> 01:43:54,102
and so on.

926
01:43:55,242 --> 01:43:58,762
In all these situations, the final

927
01:43:58,842 --> 01:44:02,542
identification is interesting, but the

928
01:44:02,602 --> 01:44:06,442
process that led to the identification can

929
01:44:06,542 --> 01:44:08,802
also be very informative.

930
01:44:10,282 --> 01:44:13,962
Let me give you a concrete example coming

931
01:44:14,042 --> 01:44:18,022
from SPipole. SPipole is a French citizen science

932
01:44:18,082 --> 01:44:19,382
program developed by the

933
01:44:20,222 --> 01:44:22,162
National History Museum in Paris.

934
01:44:24,362 --> 01:44:27,782
In this citizen program, participants

935
01:44:27,822 --> 01:44:31,582
photograph insects visiting flowers, identifying

936
01:44:31,682 --> 01:44:33,462
them with a free access key,

937
01:44:35,522 --> 01:44:39,442
and then submit their identification and their picture

938
01:44:39,522 --> 01:44:40,582
to the SPipole.

939
01:44:41,542 --> 01:44:44,982
The Expert 3 development team implemented a system

940
01:44:45,602 --> 01:44:49,482
to record the identification pathways followed

941
01:44:49,542 --> 01:44:50,762
by participants.

942
01:44:51,842 --> 01:44:55,622
This made it possible to analyze the sequence of character

943
01:44:55,702 --> 01:44:59,602
choice, identify errors, collect feedback, and

944
01:44:59,662 --> 01:45:00,722
generate metrics

945
01:45:01,582 --> 01:45:05,062
such as the number of character used and/or the frequency of

946
01:45:05,122 --> 01:45:05,882
backtracking.

947
01:45:07,322 --> 01:45:11,282
So the identification session itself contains valuable

948
01:45:11,342 --> 01:45:12,142
information.

949
01:45:15,362 --> 01:45:18,682
But the limitation in this example with SPipole

950
01:45:19,302 --> 01:45:22,562
was that we record the

951
01:45:22,622 --> 01:45:26,322
identification session in a specific closed format.

952
01:45:27,322 --> 01:45:31,062
And this raised the question, how could we share

953
01:45:31,162 --> 01:45:34,601
such information using an open standard?

954
01:45:38,282 --> 01:45:41,962
So what is to store and to share to analyze identification

955
01:45:42,062 --> 01:45:42,682
sessions?

956
01:45:44,342 --> 01:45:45,962
In case of a single access

957
01:45:46,802 --> 01:45:47,062
key,

958
01:45:48,222 --> 01:45:52,182
it can be represented as a graph, and when a user follows such a

959
01:45:52,282 --> 01:45:56,102
key, the identification trajectory is a path through

960
01:45:56,162 --> 01:45:56,722
that graph.

961
01:45:57,622 --> 01:46:01,542
So one could say, if SDD can represent a

962
01:46:01,622 --> 01:46:05,582
single access key, perhaps it can also represent

963
01:46:07,062 --> 01:46:07,502
a path.

964
01:46:09,322 --> 01:46:12,942
But is an identification session really

965
01:46:13,042 --> 01:46:15,002
only a path through a graph?

966
01:46:16,022 --> 01:46:19,622
The answer is clearly no. And this is the

967
01:46:19,702 --> 01:46:20,362
central

968
01:46:21,222 --> 01:46:23,402
point of our proposing.

969
01:46:26,702 --> 01:46:29,942
An identification session is more than a path.

970
01:46:30,542 --> 01:46:34,142
We need to know, for example, who performed the identification and what

971
01:46:34,242 --> 01:46:36,402
specimen was being identified.

972
01:46:37,262 --> 01:46:40,482
We may also want to record the observations made by the user,

973
01:46:41,242 --> 01:46:43,402
and the user can express uncertainty,

974
01:46:45,602 --> 01:46:46,042
correct

975
01:46:47,242 --> 01:46:50,302
backtracking, also to modify previous response.

976
01:46:51,682 --> 01:46:54,542
And in hybrid identification process, part of the

977
01:46:54,582 --> 01:46:58,522
identifications may come from AI assistance.

978
01:47:01,822 --> 01:47:03,162
So the identification

979
01:47:04,002 --> 01:47:07,922
session is a combination of context, observation,

980
01:47:08,442 --> 01:47:12,082
and navigation through an identification process.

981
01:47:15,202 --> 01:47:17,942
What cover the current SDD standard?

982
01:47:18,842 --> 01:47:22,822
SDD was designed to represent descriptive data and also single

983
01:47:22,882 --> 01:47:25,222
access key, as presented here.

984
01:47:26,842 --> 01:47:26,982
So

985
01:47:28,082 --> 01:47:31,282
SDD already provides a way to represent the graph of an

986
01:47:31,362 --> 01:47:34,802
identification key, and we are not proposing to replace

987
01:47:35,742 --> 01:47:37,722
the existing representation of key.

988
01:47:38,742 --> 01:47:42,082
Rather, we are asking whether SDD can be

989
01:47:42,162 --> 01:47:46,022
extended so that this exchange format can also

990
01:47:46,062 --> 01:47:48,822
describe what happens when the key is used.

991
01:47:53,702 --> 01:47:56,882
So if current SDD doesn't support identification

992
01:47:57,242 --> 01:47:57,842
sessions,

993
01:47:59,122 --> 01:48:02,862
it has to be adapted, and we propose to extend

994
01:48:03,142 --> 01:48:04,882
SDD to represent

995
01:48:06,682 --> 01:48:10,002
a context, for example, the user, the specimen, the date of

996
01:48:10,062 --> 01:48:10,942
identification,

997
01:48:11,742 --> 01:48:15,502
the identification trajectory, including the question asked, the

998
01:48:15,562 --> 01:48:19,062
response given, uncertainty, correction, backtracking.

999
01:48:19,542 --> 01:48:23,362
And third, in the case of hybrid identification, information

1000
01:48:23,442 --> 01:48:26,462
about the AI component, for example, the model

1001
01:48:27,122 --> 01:48:28,902
used and its output.

1002
01:48:31,322 --> 01:48:35,022
But here we will not define all these aspects.

1003
01:48:40,402 --> 01:48:41,722
To extend SDD,

1004
01:48:42,822 --> 01:48:45,322
we could suggest to add three objects:

1005
01:48:46,902 --> 01:48:50,202
identification context, identification session, and

1006
01:48:50,282 --> 01:48:54,082
identification process. And for today's presentation, we

1007
01:48:54,142 --> 01:48:57,082
just focus on the identification session.

1008
01:49:00,602 --> 01:49:02,202
An identification session,

1009
01:49:03,962 --> 01:49:07,742
we propose to represent it as a sequence of steps.

1010
01:49:08,082 --> 01:49:11,002
A step can be a question, a response, or a result.

1011
01:49:11,682 --> 01:49:13,562
For example, we can start with the question

1012
01:49:14,702 --> 01:49:16,802
Q1, the user response

1013
01:49:17,502 --> 01:49:21,462
R1, the identification process produce a

1014
01:49:21,502 --> 01:49:25,122
result, and so on, and it's possible to have backtrack

1015
01:49:28,942 --> 01:49:30,402
So a step can be

1016
01:49:32,102 --> 01:49:33,802
a question, a response, and a result.

1017
01:49:33,862 --> 01:49:34,702
And a response,

1018
01:49:39,942 --> 01:49:43,582
in case of qualitative question, a response may contain one state or

1019
01:49:43,662 --> 01:49:47,422
several possible states together with a confidence value.

1020
01:49:48,482 --> 01:49:52,202
For quantitative question, the response may be a numerical value or

1021
01:49:52,262 --> 01:49:54,722
interval or another expression together with

1022
01:49:55,562 --> 01:49:57,342
information about accuracy.

1023
01:49:58,142 --> 01:49:59,522
The important point here

1024
01:50:00,462 --> 01:50:04,402
is that we should not lose the uncertainty expressed by the observer

1025
01:50:04,442 --> 01:50:06,402
when the session is stored.

1026
01:50:08,422 --> 01:50:12,282
The terms confidence, accuracy, and compatibility, of course, will

1027
01:50:12,342 --> 01:50:15,442
need precise semantics in a future standard.

1028
01:50:18,182 --> 01:50:21,022
A step can also be a result,

1029
01:50:22,222 --> 01:50:25,842
and a result leads to three possible outcomes: a new

1030
01:50:25,882 --> 01:50:29,482
questions, a end, meaning that the identification

1031
01:50:29,542 --> 01:50:30,482
process terminates,

1032
01:50:31,682 --> 01:50:35,482
or in case of backtrack, it leads to a previous question,

1033
01:50:35,582 --> 01:50:38,202
typically to modify a previous response.

1034
01:50:41,922 --> 01:50:42,462
And when the

1035
01:50:43,542 --> 01:50:47,302
result is end, the identification may

1036
01:50:47,362 --> 01:50:51,282
produce one or several taxa together with information such

1037
01:50:51,382 --> 01:50:53,962
as compatibility or probability.

1038
01:50:54,982 --> 01:50:58,962
But end does not necessarily mean that a successful identification has been

